        "RAII ties a resource to an owner object's lifetime. std::unique_ptr<int> from <memory> owns a single int and releases it when the owner is destroyed, including normal block exit and stack unwinding due to an exception. auto p=std::make_unique<int>(7); creates an owner without explicit new. Access the value with *p. Manually deleting an object owned by unique_ptr is unnecessary and dangerous.\n\nunique_ptr ownership cannot be copied. auto q=std::move(p); transfers it to another unique_ptr; include <utility>. In this particular move, p becomes empty and q owns the original object. std::move itself is a cast; the type's move operation performs the actual transfer. reset() releases the managed object and leaves the owner empty.",
